course: dictionary
lesson: 4297
title: Feelings after loss: grieve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To grieve means to feel very deep sadness, especially when someone you love has died. You can also grieve for a lost pet, a home or a friendship. Look at the words around it to be sure. «Megan grieved for her old dog for months.» The word for is a clue: she was sad about losing something she loved.
explain: Grief is a normal reaction to loss, and it takes time. People show it in different ways. «Some cry, some go quiet, some keep busy; no tears does not mean no love.» So a quiet person can be grieving just as much as someone who cries.
explain: Grieving can also describe people. «Many grieving children are scared of forgetting.» Here grieving tells you the children are feeling this deep sadness. Try swapping in sad: the sentence still works, but grieving is stronger, because it is sadness that comes from a loss.
explain: In very old or formal English, «it grieves me» means it makes me very sad. You may meet this in old stories. Today people say "it makes me so sad" instead.
fact: Grieve means to feel very deep sadness, especially after someone you love has died.
fact: You can also grieve for a lost pet, a home or a friendship.
fact: «Grieving» describes people who are feeling this sadness, as in «grieving people».
fact: Grieving takes time, and talking to a trusted adult can help.
fact: People grieve in different ways: crying, being quiet, keeping busy, feeling angry, or even laughing at a memory.
exercise: «Megan grieved for her old dog for months.» What does grieved mean here? | Forgot all about the dog at once | *Felt very deep sadness about losing something she loved | Bought a new dog straight away | Ran around the garden happily
exercise: «Some cry, some go quiet, some keep busy; no tears does not mean no love.» What does this tell you? | Quiet people never love anyone | *People grieve in different ways, and quiet does not mean they feel less | Grieving people must always be busy | Only people who cry are really sad
exercise: Which word in «Both are frightened and both families are grieving.» means feeling deep sadness after a loss? | frightened | both | families | *grieving
test: Which meaning fits grieve best? | To run very fast | To feel happy about a holiday | To shout at a friend | *To feel very deep sadness after a loss
test: In «Being noisy at funerals and memorials can hurt grieving people for a long time.» what does grieving people mean? | *People who are feeling deep sadness after a loss | People who are very noisy | People who are laughing at funny films | People who are going to a party
exam: Priya's cat went missing and never came home, and weeks later she still feels heavy and sad. Which word best describes how Priya feels? | shouting | *grieving | laughing | sleeping
